ons across membership transitions, snapshot transport failures, storage crash atomicity and session deduplication remain open.'],rationale='Representative formation, authority change and old-work handling are traced through actual membership, recovery, persistence and completion owners. Usable navigation does not certify these paths.',formation=dict(explanation='The leader indexes proposals and aggregates per-voter/witness match acknowledgments into current-term commitment; followers validate the preceding term and protect the committed prefix. Commit propagates via replication and bounded heartbeats. Engine exports/persists state and queues committed entries to RSM, whose callbacks complete proposals and expose applied position. For reads, current-term commitment precedes distinct-voter heartbeat confirmation and prefix release; publication then feeds exact-context local batches, which additionally wait for application.',behavior_ids=['B-replicate','B-read-qualification','B-read-publication','B-persist','B-apply','B-client-read'],fact_ids=['F-committed','F-read-status'],source_ids=['src-quorum-commit','src-read-release','src-read-queue','src-update-order','src-rsm-application','src-read-consumer']),context=dict(explanation='Election ticks campaign only for eligible nodes with no committed-but-unapplied entries. Available votes and up-to-date logs qualify support; known-peer response filtering and term dispatch precede aggregation. Higher terms, lost quorum and self-removal can remove authority; transfer waits for a full member to catch up and has a timeout. Reset discards pending read support and remote progress but preserves log commitment. New leadership appends a no-op and reconstructs pending config state. Membership changes are applied by the RSM then reflected in Raft under raftMu; recovery reconstructs snapshot membership and saved term/vote/log before later formation.',behavior_ids=['B-authority','B-membership','B-recovery','B-persist'],fact_ids=['F-committed','F-read-status'],source_ids=['src-authority-reset','src-term-election','src-peer-boundary','src-authority-timers','src-transfer','src-rsm-config','src-config-apply','src-rsm-recovery','src-new-raft']),connection=dict(explanation='Support is owned by the current term and installed membership. Authority transitions clear volatile votes/read support/progress, while persisted term/vote and protected committed history constrain future elections and replication. Applied membership updates redefine eligible participants and quorum; election blocking prevents campaigning before committed history is consumed. Confirmed reads bridge leadership support and client consumption through request context and application position, so release and notification are separate responsibilities. Stale-term replies are rejected; forwarded pending requests have distinct context, drop/timeout handling and no implicit completion guarantee from role acquisition.',behavior_ids=['B-authority','B-membership','B-replicate','B-read-qualification','B-read-publication','B-client-read','B-apply'],fact_ids=['F-committed','F-read-status'],source_ids=['src-term-election','src-authority-reset','src-membership-raft','src-read-queue','src-read-reply','src-forward-read','src-read-consumer']))\nm=dict(version=1,target_profile=dict(system_boundary='Captured Dragonboat Go module: NodeHost/node/engine, internal Raft state machine, RSM, storage and transport integration. In-repository implementations remain in scope even where injectable.',protocol_contexts=['ClusterID/NodeID, term/vote/log, applied membership, read SystemCtx'],external_interfaces=['NodeHost.ReadIndex and RequestState.ResultC','Peer update persistence/message delivery contract','Application state-machine callbacks'],ownership=['node.raftMu serializes Raft stepping and membership callbacks','Engine saves updates and application workers consume committed tasks'],variants=['Voters, observers, witnesses','Snapshot recovery and optional on-disk/concurrent state machines'],source_ids=['src-read-api','src-node-step','src-update-order','src-membership-rules','src-new-raft'],unknowns=['Backend crash atomicity and application-specific behavior remain unread']),activities=acts,behaviors=beh,facts=facts,core_overview=core,surfaces=[dict(entry_point='raft.handleReadIndexLeaderConfirmation',disposition='mapped',behavior_ids=['B-read-publication'],reason='Remote prefix-release context substitution is not resolved by the map; selected for a sourced correlation question.',source_ids=['src-read-reply','src-read-queue'],high_consequence=False),dict(entry_point='StateMachine.update',disposition='deferred',reason='Session-managed application and deduplication are supporting responsibilities not yet deeply traced.',source_ids=['src-rsm-application'],high_consequence=True),dict(entry_point='Transport.send',disposition='deferred',reason='Loss is sourced; detailed reconnection ordering and snapshot transfer remain open.',source_ids=['src-transport-loss'],high_consequence=True)])\njson.dump(m,open('audit-map.json','w'),indent=2)\nq=dict(question='When a leader confirms a later queued ReadIndex context and releases an earlier remote request in the same prefix, does publication preserve the earlier request context and origin through the emitted reply and recipient readiness?',importance='Mis-correlated read results can retire leader-side pending work without notifying the originating local batch, producing lost completion until timeout despite quorum confirmation. This is a local correlation responsibility, not an asserted consensus-safety violation.',source_ids=['src-read-queue','src-read-reply','src-forward-read','src-read-consumer','src-prefix-test','src-read-output-test','src-read-api'],participants=['Leader','Remote read requester','Voting heartbeat responder'],objects=['readStatus','ReadIndexResp','ReadyToRead'],contexts=['Stable voting membership','Same leader term','Multiple distinct admitted contexts'],event_paths=['Peer.ReadIndex -> follower forwarding -> leader queue','Later-context heartbeat quorum -> prefix release -> remote reply -> follower readiness'],activity_classes=['A1','A5'],behavior_ids=['B-read-qualification','B-read-publication'],fact_ids=['F-read-status'],supporting_behavior_ids={'B-client-read':'Exact-context batch consumer and actual request producer','B-authority':'Term/role filtering and reset boundaries','B-persist':'Message publication/update completion order'},obligation_relation_kind='consumption',counterevidence=['Local release uses s.ctx correctly.','Existing sequential read test preserves context for non-overlapped requests.','Current-term admission, peer filtering and applied-index gate protect separate premises.'],unknowns=['A fixed legal multi-request history must reach prefix release and independently observe reply/readiness identity; no execution yet.'],priority=2,trigger_rationale='confirm preserves each released status ctx/from and removes the prefix, but remote publication substitutes the confirming message context. Smaller source investigation found an exact-context consumer and test expectations; a narrow deterministic peer schedule can discriminate without a client deadline.',disposition='ready_for_check',preferred_check='controlled_schedule')\ncid='C-read-context-preservation'\nclaim=dict(id=cid,kind='obligation',concern='implementation_semantics',description='For each admitted remote ReadIndex request released by a same-term leader quorum confirmation, publication of its read index must retain that request\\\\'s original SystemCtx and recipient identity, including when a later context confirms a queued prefix.',source_ids=q['source_ids'],scope=dict(description='Remote read-result identity at quorum prefix release in stable membership and authority; does not require eventual global progress.',assumptions=['Non-Byzantine participants and authentic generated protocol messages','Distinct nonzero read contexts and legal message loss; no fabricated ac